Para. 1 let. f — Inserted by No I of the FA of 18 March 2016, in force since 1 Jan. 2017 (AS 2016 3207; BBl 2014 4909).
Para. 1 let. g — Inserted by No I of the FA of 18 March 2016, in force since 1 Jan. 2017 (AS 2016 3207; BBl 2014 4909).
Para. 2 let. a — Amended by No I of the FA of 18 March 2016, in force since 1 Jan. 2017 (AS 2016 3207; BBl 2014 4909).
|

:INFO
Art. 39 Education and training
1 The Confederation provides subsidies for the education and training of forestry personnel according to Articles 52–59 of the Vocational and Professional Education and Training Act of 13 December 2002.
2 In derogation from paragraph 1 it assumes up to 50 percent of the occupation-specific costs, in particular for the on-site practical training of forestry personnel and creation of teaching material for forestry personnel.
3 …
|

:NOTE
Para. 1 — SR 412.10
Para. 1 — Amended by Annex No II 6 of the Vocational and Professional Education and Training Act of 13 December 2002, in force since 1 Jan. 2004 (AS 2003 4557; BBl 2000 5686).
Para. 2 — Amended by Annex No II 6 of the Vocational and Professional Education and Training Act of 13 December 2002, in force since 1 Jan. 2004 (AS 2003 4557; BBl 2000 5686).
Para. 3 — Repealed by No I of the FA of 18 March 2016, with effect from 1 Jan. 2017 (AS 2016 3207; BBl 2014 4909).
|

:INFO
Art. 40 Investment credits
1 The Confederation may grant interest-free or low-interest repayable credits:
a. as building loans;
b. for the financing of the residual costs of measures eligible for subsidy under Articles 36, 37 and 38a paragraph 1 letter b;
c. for the acquisition of forestry vehicles, machines and equipment and for the creation of forestry installations.
2 The loans are limited in term.
3 Loans are only granted on the application of the canton. If a debtor does not meet his repayment obligation, the relevant canton shall assume responsibility for the repayment in his place.
4 Repayments shall be used to fund new investment credits.
|

:NOTE
Para. 1 let. b — Amended by No II 30 of the Federal Act of 6 Oct. 2006 on the New System of Financial Equalisation and Division of Tasks between the Confederation and the Cantons (NFE), in force since 1 Jan. 2008 (AS 2007 5779; BBl 2005 6029).
|

:INFO
Art. 41 Provision of subsidies
1 The Federal Assembly shall approve by simple federal degree a temporary four-year guarantee credit for the provision of subsidies and credits.
2 Subsidies for the response to extraordinary natural events are limited in time according to the duration of the corresponding measures.
|

:NOTE
Art. 41 — Amended by No II 30 of the Federal Act of 6 Oct. 2006 on the New System of Financial Equalisation and Division of Tasks between the Confederation and the Cantons (NFE), in force since 1 Jan. 2008 (AS 2007 5779; BBl 2005 6029).
Para. 1 — Term in accordance with Annex No 9 of the FA of 19 March 2021, in force since 1 Jan. 2022 (AS 2021 662; BBl 2020 349). This amendment has been made in the provisions specified in the AS.

:PATH
Section 3 Further Measures
|

:NOTE
Inserted by Annex No 8 of the FA of 21 June 2013, in force since 1 Jan. 2017 (AS 2015 3631; BBl 2009 8533).
|

:INFO
Art. 41a Declaration of origin
1 The Federal Council may issue regulations on the voluntary declaration of origin of forest products and their processed products in order to promote quality and sales.
2 Registration, protection of labels, procedures and legal protection are governed by the Agriculture Act of 29 April 1998.
3 The Federal Council may transfer responsibility for the above to third parties.
|

:NOTE
Art. 41a — Inserted by No I of the FA of 27 Sept. 2024, in force since 1 Aug. 2025 (AS 2025 403; BBl 2024 971, 1126).
Para. 2 — SR 910.1
Para. 2 — Amended by Annex No 2 of the FA of 16 June 2023, in force since 1 Jan. 2025 (AS 2024 623; BBl 2020 3955).
Para. 3 — Inserted by Annex No 2 of the FA of 16 June 2023, in force since 1 Jan. 2025 (AS 2024 623; BBl 2020 3955).
|

:INFO
Art. 41b Recommended prices for raw timber
1 The forest owners’ organisations may at national or regional level issue recommended prices for raw timber that suppliers and their customers have agreed on.
2 The recommended prices shall differ according to tree species, product range and quality grades.
3 There shall be no obligation to comply with the recommended prices.
4 No recommended prices shall be stipulated for consumers.
|

:NOTE
Art. 41b — Inserted by No I of the FA of 27 Sept. 2024, in force since 1 Aug. 2025 (AS 2025 403; BBl 2024 971, 1126).

